---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ChecklistBlock from '../components/sections/ChecklistBlock.astro';
import FitBlock from '../components/sections/FitBlock.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/sections/CtaBand.astro';

// The "four businesses, one story" pattern. Other businesses are described by
// type only — a real company name goes here only once that company has signed a
// reference-site agreement. MSM may be named.
const businesses = [
  { name: 'A cabinetmaker who scaled', detail: 'built a name for top work, grew, builds kitchens' },
  { name: 'A superyacht fit-out firm', detail: 'one-off interiors, every job custom' },
  { name: 'A geotech outfit', detail: 'started by a grad who was good with clients, grew' },
  { name: 'Morris Sheetmetals — us', detail: '~15-person sheet metal shop; DocketWorks runs it' },
];

const fitItems = [
  'Around 15 staff.',
  'The real product is people’s hours — even when the invoice says fabrications, reports, or custom installations.',
  'Every job is custom; you’re not making the same product over and over.',
  'A couple of thousand jobs a year, so quick data entry matters.',
  'Separate accounting — Xero is your books; DocketWorks isn’t.',
  'Materials sold near cost; the profit’s in the hours.',
  'Roughly one active job per staff member, mostly self-contained.',
];

const roadmap = [
  'Timesheets on a phone or tablet',
  'Leads / pre-sales tracking (coming soon)',
  'Smarter handling of repeat jobs',
  'GPS / site-location features',
  'AI to help with quoting and following your job steps',
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Who it’s for — DocketWorks"
  description="For shops with one story: you came up doing the work, you built a name, you scaled — and now the admin’s threatening to drown you. If that’s you, you’ll love it. If it isn’t, we’ll tell you."
>
  <section class="bg-primary-50 py-20 md:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[var(--max-w-site)] px-6">
      <h1 class="max-w-3xl text-3xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-primary-900 md:text-4xl">
        Who it’s for
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-primary-700">
        You were great at the work. You built a name for it. You scaled. Now the
        admin’s threatening to drown you, and the place wobbles whenever one key
        person’s away.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-primary-700">
        We keep meeting that story. A cabinetmaker who scaled. A superyacht fit-out
        firm. A geotech outfit. A sheet metal shop — us. Four versions of one thing,
        and we think there are more.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {businesses.map((b) => (
          <li class="rounded-xl border border-primary-200 bg-white p-5">
            <p class="font-semibold text-primary-900">{b.name}</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-primary-600">{b.detail}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ChecklistBlock
    heading="The shape it fits"
    lead="Built around how MSM works — the closer your shop looks to this, the better the fit."
    items={fitItems}
    caveat="Every business is different somewhere; the further off this, the more the fit gets questionable."
  />

  <FitBlock heading="It might not be you — and we’ll tell you so." bg="light">
    <p>
      We obsess about one kind of business — the story above. If that’s you, you’ll
      love it: it already knows how a shop like yours runs, so there’s nothing to
      set up and no settings to fiddle with.
    </p>
    <p>
      If your shop works in a fundamentally different way — say you need deep
      jobs-inside-jobs sequencing — a tool with more switches will suit you better,
      or honestly, Asana or Monday. We’d rather point you there than have you find
      out the hard way. We’re not trying to be the best job software for most shops;
      we’re trying to be the best for shops with this story.
    </p>
  </FitBlock>

  {/* Who built this */}
  <section class="bg-white py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[var(--max-w-site)] px-6">
      <div class="grid items-center gap-10 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-primary-900 md:text-3xl">Who built this</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-primary-700">
            Morris Sheetmetals is a working ~15-person sheet metal shop. DocketWorks
            is the system it runs on — built from the inside, by the people doing the
            work. That’s why it’s quick, why there’s no fluff, why every field on the
            screen is there for a reason.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-primary-700">
            You’re not buying a software company’s guess at how your business works.
            You’re buying the tool another shop built for itself.
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure>
          <img
            src="/placeholder-msm-shopfloor.svg"
            alt="The Morris Sheetmetals shop floor — people doing the work"
            class="w-full rounded-xl border border-primary-200"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-primary-500">The Morris Sheetmetals shop floor.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Where it's headed */}
  <section class="bg-primary-50 py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[var(--max-w-site)] px-6">
      <h2 class="max-w-2xl text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-primary-900 md:text-3xl">Where it’s headed</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-primary-700">
        It’s young. Parts of the system still assume how MSM works, and shaping it
        to a new shop takes time. Here’s what we’re building next — things that exist
        in the system but aren’t yet at MSM’s “faster than paper” bar:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {roadmap.map((r) => (
          <li class="flex gap-3 rounded-lg border border-primary-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-base text-primary-800">
            <span class="text-accent-500">→</span>{r}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand headline="Think that’s your shop? Have a look." />
</BaseLayout>
